      "text": "First, we start with the given equation:\n\\[\n(x - 5)^2 = 9\n\\]\n\nNext, we take the square root of both sides to solve for \\(x\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{(x - 5)^2} = \\sqrt{9}\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\nx - 5 = \\pm 3\n\\]\n\nWe now have two cases to consider:\n1. \\(x - 5 = 3\\)\n2. \\(x - 5 = -3\\)\n\nSolving each case separately:\n\n**Case 1:**\n\\[\nx - 5 = 3\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 3 + 5\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 8\n\\]\n\n**Case 2:**\n\\[\nx - 5 = -3\n\\]\n\\[\nx = -3 + 5\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 2\n\\]\n\nThus, the solutions to the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\) are \\(x = 8\\) and \\(x = 2\\).\n\nTo find the sum of the roots, we add these solutions together:\n\\[\n8 + 2 = 10\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the roots is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{10}\n\\]",
